<section class="introduction">
  <h1>ObjectFramework Guides <span>(v0.1.0)</span></h1>
  <p>These guides teach you to build Ruby applications from collaborating objects. Start with a plain use case, grow it into an order-confirmation application, and understand how its objects, transactions, HTTP, and gRPC fit together.</p>
</section>
<div class="guide-index">
  <% @guides.group_by(&:section).each do |section, entries| -%>
    <section><h2><%= h(section) %></h2><dl>
      <% entries.each do |entry| -%>
        <dt><a href="<%= entry.slug %>.html"><%= h(entry.title) %></a></dt>
        <dd><%= h(entry.summary) %></dd>
      <% end -%>
    </dl></section>
  <% end -%>
</div>
<section class="reading-note"><h2>Read the code alongside the guides</h2><p>The examples are versioned with the framework and run in its test suite. When a guide shows a full example, its source link opens the exact program. Explanations also point to implementation tests, so you can follow a claim to executable evidence.</p><p>Ruby Box, Ractor, and JIT features are optional. The core framework runs on Ruby 4.0.8; SQLite is its sole optional runtime gem.</p></section>
